Case 1: the reported queries -- GROUP BY on tbl_a alone, and the same with a one-row cross join     

===================================================
colb    cnt    
1     2     
2     2     
3     2     

Query plan:
iscan
    class: a node[?]
    index: idx_colb (covers)
    sort:  ? asc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select a.colb, count(*) from tbl_a a group by a.colb using index a.idx_colb
/* ---> skip GROUP BY */
===================================================
colb    cnt    
1     2     
2     2     
3     2     

Query plan:
nl-join (cross join)
    outer: iscan
               class: a node[?]
               index: idx_colb (covers)
               cost:  ? card ?
    inner: sscan
               class: c node[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    sort:  ? asc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select a.colb, count(*) from tbl_a a, tbl_c c group by a.colb using index a.idx_colb
/* ---> skip GROUP BY */
===================================================
    
Case 2: an inner join under a cross join, the index of tbl_a is two joins down     

===================================================
colb    cnt    
1     3     
2     2     
3     2     

Query plan:
nl-join (cross join)
    outer: idx-join (inner join)
               outer: iscan
                          class: a node[?]
                          index: idx_colb 
                          cost:  ? card ?
               inner: iscan
                          class: b node[?]
                          index: idx_cold term[?] (covers)
                          cost:  ? card ?
               cost:  ? card ?
    inner: sscan
               class: c node[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    sort:  ? asc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select /*+ ORDERED USE_IDX */ a.colb, count(*) from tbl_a a, tbl_b b, tbl_c c where b.cold=a.cola group by a.colb using index a.idx_colb, b.idx_cold
/* ---> skip GROUP BY */
===================================================
    
Case 3: left outer join, a tbl_a row without a match in tbl_b is counted in its group     

===================================================
colb    cnt    cnt_b    
1     3     3     
2     3     2     
3     2     2     

Query plan:
idx-join (left outer join)
    outer: iscan
               class: a node[?]
               index: idx_colb 
               cost:  ? card ?
    inner: iscan
               class: b node[?]
               index: idx_cold term[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    sort:  ? asc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select /*+ USE_IDX */ a.colb, count(*), count(b.colc) from tbl_a a left outer join tbl_b b on b.cold=a.cola group by a.colb using index a.idx_colb, b.idx_cold
/* ---> skip GROUP BY */
===================================================
    
Case 4: hash join, the GROUP BY is still sorted     

===================================================
colb    cnt    
1     3     
2     2     
3     2     

Query plan:
temp(group by)
    subplan: hash-join (inner join)
                 edge:  term[?]
                 outer: iscan
                            class: a node[?]
                            index: idx_colb 
                            cost:  ? card ?
                 inner: sscan
                            class: b node[?]
                            cost:  ? card ?
                 cost:  ? card ?
    sort:  ? asc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select /*+ ORDERED USE_HASH */ a.colb, count(*) from tbl_a a, tbl_b b where b.cold=a.cola group by a.colb using index a.idx_colb, b.idx_cold
===================================================
    
Case 5: right outer join, the GROUP BY is still sorted and the tbl_b row without a match makes the NULL group     

===================================================
colb    cnt    
null     1     
1     3     
2     2     
3     2     

Query plan:
temp(group by)
    subplan: nl-join (left outer join)
                 edge:  term[?]
                 outer: sscan
                            class: b node[?]
                            cost:  ? card ?
                 inner: sscan
                            class: a node[?]
                            sargs: term[?]
                            cost:  ? card ?
                 cost:  ? card ?
    sort:  ? asc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select a.colb, count(*) from tbl_a a right outer join tbl_b b on b.cold=a.cola group by a.colb using index a.idx_colb
===================================================
    
Case 6: partitioned table as the inner, the GROUP BY is still sorted     

===================================================
colb    cnt    
1     3     
2     2     
3     2     

Query plan:
temp(group by)
    subplan: idx-join (inner join)
                 outer: iscan
                            class: a node[?]
                            index: idx_colb 
                            cost:  ? card ?
                 inner: iscan
                            class: d node[?]
                            index: idx_colg term[?] (covers)
                            cost:  ? card ?
                 cost:  ? card ?
    sort:  ? asc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select /*+ ORDERED USE_IDX */ a.colb, count(*) from tbl_a a, tbl_d d where d.colg=a.cola group by a.colb using index a.idx_colb
